RG DS OS: a 64 MiB default CMA region (BananaLinux/ROCKNIX's patch made it 256 MiB)

RG DS OS has no vendor display stack: the direct present's scanout buffers are a few MiB of CMA, and the GPU
(panfrost) allocates from system memory. 64 MiB instead of 256 saves about 60 ms of boot (the larger region's setup
took 88 ms) and leaves 192 MiB to the games. Was two patches until 2026-11-23 (this one at 256 MiB, then
dts-patches/0005 cutting it to 64).

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x-base.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x-base.dtsi
index fd2214b6fad4..6863f5af526d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x-base.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x-base.dtsi
@@ -184,6 +184,13 @@ scmi_shmem: shmem@10f000 {
 			reg = <0x0 0x0010f000 0x0 0x100>;
 			no-map;
 		};
+        linux,cma {
+			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
+			reusable;
+			size = <0x0 0x4000000>;
+			alignment = <0x0 0x400000>;
+			linux,cma-default;
+		};
 	};
 
 	timer {
